invariant: INV-26
file: quic.c
catches: test/docker-aes-runtime-qemu.sh
reason: an AES=runtime QUIC session seals its Initial packets under the
  answer that the AES instructions are present, whatever its caller's
  probe found, so a session on a CPU without them runs the instructions
  on its first packet and dies of SIGILL. Both ciphers compute the same
  packet, so every loop passes on a CPU with the instructions, and
  bin/aes_runtime_test, which counts the calls into aes_hw.c, links no
  quic.c. test/aes-runtime-qemu.sh runs the handshakes of the absent
  answer on a CPU model without AES-NI or PCLMULQDQ.
  The lane skips without docker, and this then reports unguarded rather
  than caught.

--- old
    int rc = QUIC_INITIAL_SEAL(q->t.cfg.aes_instructions, CH_QUIC_SELF(q), version, q->initial_dcid,
--- new
    int rc = QUIC_INITIAL_SEAL(CH_AES_INSTRUCTIONS_PRESENT, CH_QUIC_SELF(q), version, q->initial_dcid,
